<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8">
  <meta name="description" content="Nunjucks engine — boundary validation pattern: zod schema narrows untrusted req.query from unknown into a typed domain value before any template runs.">
  <title>Boundary Validation — Nunjucks</title>
  <style>
    body { font-family: system-ui, -apple-system, sans-serif; max-width: 900px; margin: 60px auto; padding: 0 24px; color: #2c3e50; line-height: 1.6; }
    h1 { margin: 0 0 8px; font-size: 1.6rem; }
    h2 { color: #3498db; border-bottom: 2px solid #3498db; padding-bottom: 6px; margin-top: 32px; font-size: 1.1rem; }
    .result { background: #d4edda; border: 1px solid #27ae60; padding: 16px; border-radius: 8px; margin: 16px 0; }
    .result p { margin: 4px 0; }
    code { font-family: ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Consolas, monospace; background: #f3f4f6; padding: 1px 6px; border-radius: 4px; font-size: 0.9em; }
    .try { background: #f8f9fa; padding: 16px; border-radius: 8px; }
    .try li { margin: 4px 0; }
    a { color: #3498db; }
  </style>
</head>
<body>
  <h1>Boundary Validation</h1>
  <p>Untrusted input arrives as <code>unknown</code>. The route narrows it through a <a href="https://zod.dev">zod</a> schema before the engine ever sees it. This is the canonical pattern: <code>unknown</code> &rarr; schema parse &rarr; typed domain value &rarr; render.</p>

  <section class="result">
    <h2>Parsed &amp; validated</h2>
    <p><strong>name</strong>: <code>{{ name }}</code></p>
    <p><strong>count</strong>: <code>{{ count }}</code></p>
  </section>

  <div class="try">
    <h2>Try variants</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><a href="/boundary?name=Alice&amp;count=5">/boundary?name=Alice&amp;count=5</a> — valid</li>
      <li><a href="/boundary?name=&amp;count=0">/boundary?name=&amp;count=0</a> — empty name, non-positive count → <code>400</code></li>
      <li><a href="/boundary?name=Alice">/boundary?name=Alice</a> — missing count → <code>400</code></li>
      <li><a href="/boundary?name=Alice&amp;count=abc">/boundary?name=Alice&amp;count=abc</a> — non-numeric count → <code>400</code></li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <p><a href="/">← Back to index</a></p>
</body>
</html>